description:
Auckland Festival of Photography 2026 presents a suite of outdoor exhibitions in response to the theme this year, Movement [Kori], including:&nbsp;

An exclusive suite of works from Taiwan by Shen Chao-Liang, Taipei based award winning artist.
Mayumi Suzuki's 'The Tide's Gift II", a long-term project series, with a revised curated selection of images.
A presentation of an archival series, a selection of portraits from the "Up Against the Wall" Photo Collection (2001): Deborah Smith; Mark Smith; Minka Firth (d).
Cathy Carter's 'Zones of Immanence' environmental series, a selection of images.&nbsp;
NZ Herald photographers sharing their work for the theme.
Award winning photojournalist, Andrew Cornaga, Photosport focusing on the 'Beautiful Game'.
An exclusive presentation of music photography taken in New Zealand by leading professionals and amateurs alike.
A suite of works from artist residency in Hainan, China by Bronislaw Kōzka, Melbourne based artist.
An exclusive suite of works from Ukranian artist, Roman Butym, who continues to create his work in exile from his home country.&nbsp;
